Make Tolkara Management Brighter Pocket Companion: Brighter Shores, found in Steam.

Built by tools/make_companion.sh from the prepared tree, the Mac setup app is Brighter
Pocket's one-click setup. It is named Brighter Pocket Companion, with its own bundle ID and its
own folder in Application Support, so a Tolkara Management on the same Mac keeps its state;
its Swift module keeps its name, so the platform's unit tests (tools/test_management.sh)
build and pass unchanged. Its links, update check and wording name Brighter Pocket's
repository and game instead of Tolkara's and World of Warcraft's. It offers only the
brighter-shores profile (and profiles the user adds): the platform's others are neither
built nor tested with this layer. A profile without a setup.source is looked for in Steam's
libraries (management/App/Core/SteamLibrary.swift, an overlay file: Steam's own library in
Application Support and those libraryfolders.vdf lists, common/<destination> or a folder in
it), again whenever the app comes to the front. Choosing a folder accepts the game's
folder, a folder in it (Steam's, whose app is in x64arm64/) or the app itself. The Play
step names the Steam sign-in the app asks for at the first start. Not an upstream
candidate as it stands: it names one game and one repository; the Steam lookup and the
folder choice are general and could go upstream on their own.

